{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2"],"primary":"c1","title":"Massachusetts limit on upfront payments at tenancy commencement","requirement":"At or before the start of a tenancy, a lessor or the lessor's agent may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay only first month's rent, last month's rent, a security deposit of no more than one month's rent, and the cost of buying and installing a new lock and key. Any other upfront charge is prohibited, including application fees.","key_value":"Upfront payments are limited to first month's rent, last month's rent, a security deposit of at most 1 month's rent, and the lock and key cost; no application fee.","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2025-08-01","end_date":null,"citation":"M.G.L. c. 186, § 15B","coverage_conditions":"Residential real property leases and tenancies in Massachusetts; applies to lessors and their agents.","exemptions":"Does not apply to leases, rentals, occupancies or tenancies of 100 days or less for a vacation or recreational purpose.","conflict_note":"c2 (D054, secondary) says licensed brokers may charge prospective tenants fees under 254 CMR 7, and its restriction refers only to the lessor. c1 (D052, official) shows that from 2025-08-01 the restriction also covers the lessor's agent. Broker fees are now governed by M.G.L. c. 112, § 87DDD½ (see c3), so c2's broader broker carve-out is not adopted. The 2025-08-01 effective date is from c1 and reflects the amended text; c2 gives no date."},{"members":["c3"],"primary":"c3","title":"Broker fees payable only by the party who engaged the broker","requirement":"Only licensed brokers or salespersons may find rental housing for prospective tenants for a fee. Any broker fee may be paid only by the party, lessor or tenant, who originally engaged and contracted with the broker or salesperson.","key_value":"Broker fee payable only by the party who engaged the broker","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2025-08-01","end_date":null,"citation":"M.G.L. c. 112, § 87DDD½","coverage_conditions":"Applies to licensed real estate brokers and salespersons finding rental dwelling accommodations in Massachusetts.","exemptions":null,"conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
